response:
**Gates before launch.** First I confirm that `spe/predictions/r04.yaml` and `spe/plans/r04.md` are committed. They are, from 10 minutes ago. Gate 1 is the grader selftest. `grade.py` must score the oracle `spe/evals/tasks/answers.json` at 50/50 on both `label.category` and `label.priority`. It must fail every ticket for an empty prediction file and for a file with shifted labels. The selftest also checks that `answers.json` has 50 entries, because the eval set was 40 tickets before this round. Gate 2 is the control. I regrade round 3's saved runs with this round's `grade.py` and compare the result to round 3's measured numbers in `spe/prediction-log.md`. Any difference means the grader changed. In that case I halt and report to you, and I do not launch. Gate 3 is the dry run. I run the script with `args.only` set to 3 cells, for example `["B:<id1>", "C2:<id1>", "C2:<id2>"]`, and `trialsPerCell: 2`. Its output goes to `runs/r04-dry`. I check that every schema, the scan, the grade, and the judge return valid output. I also compare the measured cost per trial against the $0.04 estimate. The unmeasured cost estimate is 500 trials x $0.04 = $20, plus 50 judge calls x $0.20 = $10, plus up to 100 top-up trials x $0.04 = $4, which is about $34. If the dry-run cost puts the full run over $40, I stop and ask you. If all three gates pass, I save the script as `spe/evals/harness/r04-workflow.js` and commit it locally with no push. Then I launch it with `{ ticketIds: [<the 50 IDs listed from spe/evals/tasks/tickets/>], capUsd: 40 }`.

Some details were missing, so I chose defaults. The product runner is `node triage/bin/run.js` with `--model`, `--prompt`, `--tools`, `--ticket`, `--out`, and `--trace`. Tickets are at `spe/evals/tasks/tickets/<id>.md`. `grade.py` takes `--answers` and `--pred` and prints JSON. All of these sit in `CONFIGS` and `args`, so they are easy to change.

```js
export const meta = {
  name: 'spe-triage-r04',
  description: 'SPE eval for triage: configs B and C2, 50 tickets, 5 trials per cell, code grader first, Opus tone judge, top-up of split cells, failure analysis and completeness critic, $40 spend cap.',
  phases: [
    { title: 'Trials' },
    { title: 'Scan' },
    { title: 'Grade' },
    { title: 'Top-up' },
    { title: 'Judge' },
    { title: 'Synthesis' },
  ],
}

// ---- Round and arguments ----
const ROUND = 4
const RR = `r${String(ROUND).padStart(2, '0')}`
const DRY = Array.isArray(args.only) && args.only.length > 0
const RUN_DIR = args.runDir ?? `runs/${RR}${DRY ? '-dry' : ''}`
const TICKET_DIR = args.ticketDir ?? 'spe/evals/tasks/tickets'
const TRIALS_PER_CELL = args.trialsPerCell ?? 5
const EXPECTED_TICKETS = args.expectedTickets ?? 50
const TOPUP_PER_CELL = args.topUpPerCell ?? 5
const TOPUP_MAX_TRIALS = args.topUpMaxTrials ?? 100
const CONCURRENCY = args.concurrency ?? 10
const GRADE_CHUNK = args.gradeChunk ?? 50
// The cap covers triage API spend (measured by the runner) and Opus judge calls (estimated).
const CAP_USD = args.capUsd ?? 40
const EST_TRIAL_USD = args.estTrialUsd ?? 0.04 // unmeasured, replaced by the runner's reported usd
const EST_JUDGE_USD = args.estJudgeUsd ?? 0.20 // unmeasured, one call per ticket
const TRIAGE_MODEL = args.triageModel ?? 'claude-sonnet-5-5'
const AGENT_MODEL = 'opus'

// B is the reference. C2 changes only the tool set.
const CONFIGS = {
  B: { id: 'B', model: TRIAGE_MODEL, prompt: 'triage/prompts/prompt-12.md', tools: 'triage/tools/six.json' },
  C2: { id: 'C2', model: TRIAGE_MODEL, prompt: 'triage/prompts/prompt-12.md', tools: 'triage/tools/three-plus-check-status.json' },
}

// Tickets are allowed reads. Graders, answers, harness, predictions, plans, spec, and logs are not.
const FORBIDDEN_GREP = 'spe/(evals/(graders|harness)|evals/tasks/answers|predictions|plans|spec|prediction-log|failures)'
const FORBIDDEN_RE = new RegExp(FORBIDDEN_GREP)
const KEY_RE = /spe\/evals\/(graders|tasks\/answers)/

// ---- Cells ----
const ticketIds = args.ticketIds ?? []
if (!DRY && ticketIds.length !== EXPECTED_TICKETS) {
  throw new Error(`Expected ${EXPECTED_TICKETS} ticket IDs in args.ticketIds, got ${ticketIds.length}`)
}
const allCells = []
for (const cfgId of Object.keys(CONFIGS)) for (const t of ticketIds) allCells.push(`${cfgId}:${t}`)
const cells = DRY ? args.only : allCells
for (const c of cells) {
  const [cfgId, ticket] = c.split(':')
  if (!CONFIGS[cfgId] || !ticket) throw new Error(`Bad cell id: ${c}`)
}

// ---- Budget ----
const budget = { cap: CAP_USD, spent: 0, reserved: 0, skipped: [] }
function reserve(kind, id, est) {
  if (budget.spent + budget.reserved + est > budget.cap) {
    budget.skipped.push({ kind, id, est })
    log(`SKIP ${kind} ${id}: would cross cap $${budget.cap} (spent $${budget.spent.toFixed(2)}, reserved $${budget.reserved.toFixed(2)})`)
    return false
  }
  budget.reserved += est
  return true
}
function settle(est, actual) {
  budget.reserved -= est
  budget.spent += actual
}

// ---- Helpers ----
async function inBatches(items, size, fn) {
  const out = []
  for (let i = 0; i < items.length; i += size) {
    const part = await parallel(items.slice(i, i + size).map((x) => () => fn(x)))
    out.push(...part)
  }
  return out
}
function hash(s) {
  let h = 2166136261
  for (const ch of s) { h ^= ch.charCodeAt(0); h = Math.imul(h, 16777619) }
  return h >>> 0
}
function shuffle(arr, seed) {
  const a = arr.slice()
  let x = seed || 1
  for (let i = a.length - 1; i > 0; i--) {
    x ^= x << 13; x ^= x >>> 17; x ^= x << 5; x >>>= 0
    const j = x % (i + 1)
    ;[a[i], a[j]] = [a[j], a[i]]
  }
  return a
}

// ---- Schemas ----
const TRIAL_ITEM = {
  type: 'object',
  required: ['trialId', 'status', 'label', 'reply', 'runtime_ms', 'tool_calls', 'tool_errors', 'input_tokens', 'output_tokens', 'usd', 'commands_run'],
  properties: {
    trialId: { type: 'string' },
    status: { enum: ['completed', 'harness_error', 'rate_limited'] },
    label: {
      type: 'object',
      required: ['category', 'priority'],
      properties: {
        category: { enum: ['billing', 'bug', 'how-to', 'account', 'outage', null] },
        priority: { enum: ['P1', 'P2', 'P3', 'P4', null] },
      },
    },
    reply: { type: ['string', 'null'] },
    runtime_ms: { type: 'number' },
    tool_calls: { type: 'integer' },
    tool_errors: { type: 'integer' },
    input_tokens: { type: 'integer' },
    output_tokens: { type: 'integer' },
    usd: { type: 'number' },
    commands_run: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
    error: { type: ['string', 'null'] },
  },
}
const CELL_SCHEMA = { type: 'object', required: ['trials'], properties: { trials: { type: 'array', items: TRIAL_ITEM } } }
const SCAN_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  required: ['hits', 'traced'],
  properties: {
    hits: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'object', required: ['trialId', 'path'], properties: { trialId: { type: 'string' }, path: { type: 'string' } } } },
    traced: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
  },
}
const GRADE_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  required: ['results'],
  properties: {
    results: {
      type: 'array',
      items: {
        type: 'object',
        required: ['trialId', 'category_ok', 'priority_ok', 'file_category', 'file_priority', 'grader_error'],
        properties: {
          trialId: { type: 'string' },
          category_ok: { type: 'boolean' },
          priority_ok: { type: 'boolean' },
          file_category: { type: ['string', 'null'] },
          file_priority: { type: ['string', 'null'] },
          grader_error: { type: ['string', 'null'] },
        },
      },
    },
  },
}
const JUDGE_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  required: ['scores'],
  properties: {
    scores: {
      type: 'array',
      items: {
        type: 'object',
        required: ['rid', 'tone', 'pass', 'reason'],
        properties: { rid: { type: 'string' }, tone: { type: 'integer', minimum: 1, maximum: 5 }, pass: { type: 'boolean' }, reason: { type: 'string' } },
      },
    },
  },
}
const FAILURE_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  required: ['failure_types'],
  properties: {
    failure_types: {
      type: 'array',
      items: {
        type: 'object',
        required: ['name', 'kind', 'what', 'how_to_spot', 'seen_in', 'fix'],
        properties: {
          name: { type: 'string' },
          kind: { enum: ['agent', 'grader', 'judge', 'harness', 'task'] },
          what: { type: 'string' },
          how_to_spot: { type: 'string' },
          seen_in: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
          fix: { type: 'string' },
        },
      },
    },
  },
}
const CRITIC_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  required: ['complete', 'gaps', 'ceiling_metrics', 'halt_reasons'],
  properties: {
    complete: { type: 'boolean' },
    gaps: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
    ceiling_metrics: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
    halt_reasons: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
  },
}

// ---- Trials ----
function cellPrompt(cfg, ticket, ids) {
  const cmds = ids
    .map((id) => `node triage/bin/run.js --model ${cfg.model} --prompt ${cfg.prompt} --tools ${cfg.tools} --ticket ${TICKET_DIR}/${ticket}.md --out ${RUN_DIR}/${id}.json --trace ${RUN_DIR}/${id}.trace.jsonl`)
    .join('\n')
  return `You run trials for the triage eval, round ${ROUND}. You are a runner, not a grader.

Run these commands from the repo root, one at a time, in order. Each command is one independent trial. Do not change them.
${cmds}

After each command, read only the --out file it wrote and copy its fields into your result under that trial ID. If a command exits non-zero, set status to "harness_error". Use "rate_limited" instead if the error is a 429 or an overloaded response. Put the error text in error.

You may read only these paths: triage/**, ${TICKET_DIR}/${ticket}.md, and ${RUN_DIR}/<trial id>.json for the trial IDs above. Do not open, list, or grep anything else under spe/. Do not edit any file. List every shell command you ran in commands_run.`
}

async function runCell(cell, count, tag, ph) {
  const [cfgId, ticket] = cell.split(':')
  const cfg = CONFIGS[cfgId]
  const ids = []
  for (let i = 1; i <= count; i++) {
    const trialId = `${cfgId}-${ticket}-${tag}${i}`
    if (reserve('trial', trialId, EST_TRIAL_USD)) ids.push(trialId)
  }
  if (ids.length === 0) return []
  let out
  try {
    out = await agent(cellPrompt(cfg, ticket, ids), { label: `${ph} ${cell}`, phase: ph, schema: CELL_SCHEMA, model: AGENT_MODEL })
  } catch (e) {
    for (const _ of ids) settle(EST_TRIAL_USD, EST_TRIAL_USD)
    return ids.map((trialId) => ({ trialId, cell, cfgId, ticket, tag, status: 'harness_error', error: String(e) }))
  }
  const byId = new Map((out.trials ?? []).map((t) => [t.trialId, t]))
  return ids.map((trialId) => {
    const t = byId.get(trialId)
    settle(EST_TRIAL_USD, t && typeof t.usd === 'number' ? t.usd : EST_TRIAL_USD)
    if (!t) return { trialId, cell, cfgId, ticket, tag, status: 'harness_error', error: 'missing from runner agent output' }
    return { ...t, trialId, cell, cfgId, ticket, tag }
  })
}

// ---- Scan for peeks ----
async function scan(trials, tag) {
  phase('Scan')
  // Code check first: the runner agent's own commands.
  for (const t of trials) {
    const bad = (t.commands_run ?? []).find((c) => FORBIDDEN_RE.test(c))
    if (bad) t.void = `command touched hidden path: ${bad}`
  }
  // Then the triage agent's traces.
  const res = await agent(
    `Scan round ${ROUND} trial traces for reads of hidden files. Run:
  grep -HoE '${FORBIDDEN_GREP}' ${RUN_DIR}/*-${tag}[0-9]*.trace.jsonl
Report each hit with its trial ID (the trace filename without .trace.jsonl) and the matched path. Then list every trace file that exists for that glob, as trial IDs, in traced. Do not read any file under spe/. Do not edit anything.`,
    { label: `scan ${tag}`, phase: 'Scan', schema: SCAN_SCHEMA, model: AGENT_MODEL },
  )
  const traced = new Set(res.traced)
  const byId = new Map(trials.map((t) => [t.trialId, t]))
  let leak = false
  for (const h of res.hits) {
    const t = byId.get(h.trialId)
    if (t) t.void = `trace read hidden path: ${h.path}`
    if (KEY_RE.test(h.path)) leak = true
  }
  for (const t of trials) {
    if (t.void && KEY_RE.test(t.void)) leak = true
    if (t.status === 'completed' && !t.void && !traced.has(t.trialId)) t.void = 'no trace file, peek check not possible'
  }
  const voided = trials.filter((t) => t.void).map((t) => ({ trialId: t.trialId, reason: t.void }))
  log(`Scan ${tag}: ${voided.length} trials voided${leak ? ', answer key or grader was read' : ''}`)
  return { voided, leak }
}

// ---- Code grade ----
async function grade(trials) {
  phase('Grade')
  const todo = trials.filter((t) => t.status === 'completed' && !t.void)
  const chunks = []
  for (let i = 0; i < todo.length; i += GRADE_CHUNK) chunks.push(todo.slice(i, i + GRADE_CHUNK))
  const results = await inBatches(chunks, CONCURRENCY, (chunk) =>
    agent(
      `Run the code grader for the triage eval, round ${ROUND}, on each trial file below. For each trial ID, run:
  python spe/evals/graders/grade.py --answers spe/evals/tasks/answers.json --pred ${RUN_DIR}/<trialId>.json
It prints JSON with category_ok and priority_ok. Copy the grader's output exactly. Do not grade by your own judgment. Also copy label.category and label.priority from the pred file into file_category and file_priority. If the grader errors, set grader_error to the message and set both _ok fields to false.
Trial IDs:
${chunk.map((t) => t.trialId).join('\n')}`,
      { label: `grade ${chunk[0].trialId}..`, phase: 'Grade', schema: GRADE_SCHEMA, model: AGENT_MODEL },
    ),
  )
  const byId = new Map(todo.map((t) => [t.trialId, t]))
  let graderErrors = 0
  for (const r of results.flatMap((x) => x.results)) {
    const t = byId.get(r.trialId)
    if (!t) continue
    if (r.grader_error) graderErrors++
    if (r.file_category !== t.label?.category || r.file_priority !== t.label?.priority) {
      t.status = 'harness_error'
      t.error = 'runner agent report does not match the output file'
      continue
    }
    t.grade = { category_ok: r.category_ok, priority_ok: r.priority_ok, both_ok: r.category_ok && r.priority_ok, grader_error: r.grader_error }
  }
  for (const t of todo) if (t.status === 'completed' && !t.grade) { t.status = 'harness_error'; t.error = 'not graded' }
  log(`Grade: ${todo.length} trials, ${graderErrors} grader errors`)
  return { graderErrors }
}

function valid(t) {
  return t.status === 'completed' && !t.void && t.grade && !t.grade.grader_error
}

// ---- Run ----
phase('Trials')
log(`Round ${ROUND}${DRY ? ' DRY RUN' : ''}: ${cells.length} cells x ${TRIALS_PER_CELL} trials, cap $${CAP_USD}, out ${RUN_DIR}`)
const base = (await inBatches(cells, CONCURRENCY, (c) => runCell(c, TRIALS_PER_CELL, 't', 'Trials'))).flat()

const baseScan = await scan(base, 't')
if (baseScan.leak) {
  return { round: ROUND, dry: DRY, halt: ['leaked answer key or grader read by a trial'], voided: baseScan.voided, budget }
}
const baseGrade = await grade(base)
if (baseGrade.graderErrors > 0) {
  return { round: ROUND, dry: DRY, halt: ['broken grader: grade.py errored on completed trials'], graderErrors: baseGrade.graderErrors, budget }
}

// ---- Top-up of split cells ----
phase('Top-up')
const cellStats = {}
for (const t of base.filter(valid)) {
  const s = (cellStats[t.cell] ??= { n: 0, pass: 0 })
  s.n++
  if (t.grade.both_ok) s.pass++
}
const split = Object.entries(cellStats).filter(([, s]) => s.pass > 0 && s.pass < s.n).map(([c]) => c).sort()
let topup = []
let topScan = { voided: [], leak: false }
if (DRY) {
  log(`Top-up skipped in dry run. ${split.length} split cells seen.`)
} else {
  const plan = []
  let left = TOPUP_MAX_TRIALS
  for (const c of split) {
    if (left <= 0) { log(`Top-up cap of ${TOPUP_MAX_TRIALS} trials reached. Cell ${c} gets none.`); continue }
    const k = Math.min(TOPUP_PER_CELL, left)
    plan.push([c, k])
    left -= k
  }
  log(`Top-up: ${split.length} split cells, ${plan.reduce((s, [, k]) => s + k, 0)} extra trials planned`)
  topup = (await inBatches(plan, CONCURRENCY, ([c, k]) => runCell(c, k, 'u', 'Top-up'))).flat()
  if (topup.length) {
    topScan = await scan(topup, 'u')
    if (topScan.leak) return { round: ROUND, halt: ['leaked answer key or grader read by a top-up trial'], voided: topScan.voided, budget }
    const g = await grade(topup)
    if (g.graderErrors > 0) return { round: ROUND, halt: ['broken grader during top-up'], budget }
  }
}

// ---- Judge (tone only, base trials, blind) ----
phase('Judge')
log('Judge is Opus, the same model family as the Sonnet trials. No judge from another family is available, so shared blind spots are possible.')
const byTicket = {}
for (const t of base.filter((t) => valid(t) && t.reply)) (byTicket[t.ticket] ??= []).push(t)
await inBatches(Object.keys(byTicket).sort(), CONCURRENCY, async (ticket) => {
  if (!reserve('judge', ticket, EST_JUDGE_USD)) return
  const items = shuffle(byTicket[ticket], hash(`${RR}:${ticket}`)).map((t, i) => ({ rid: `R${i + 1}`, t }))
  const replies = items.map(({ rid, t }) => `${rid}:\n"""\n${t.reply}\n"""`).join('\n\n')
  try {
    const res = await agent(
      `You judge the tone of first replies drafted by a support triage agent. Read spe/evals/graders/judge.md and follow its rubric exactly. Read the ticket at ${TICKET_DIR}/${ticket}.md. Score only tone. Category and priority are graded elsewhere.
The replies come from different setups in random order. Do not guess the setup. Do not read any other file under spe/.

${replies}`,
      { label: `judge ${ticket}`, phase: 'Judge', schema: JUDGE_SCHEMA, model: AGENT_MODEL },
    )
    const map = new Map(items.map(({ rid, t }) => [rid, t]))
    for (const s of res.scores) {
      const t = map.get(s.rid)
      if (t) t.judge = { tone: s.tone, pass: s.pass, reason: s.reason }
    }
  } finally {
    settle(EST_JUDGE_USD, EST_JUDGE_USD)
  }
})

// ---- Synthesis ----
phase('Synthesis')
function stats(list) {
  const done = list.filter(valid)
  const n = done.length
  const mean = (f) => (n ? done.reduce((s, t) => s + (f(t) ?? 0), 0) / n : null)
  const judged = done.filter((t) => t.judge)
  const rt = done.map((t) => t.runtime_ms).sort((a, b) => a - b)
  return {
    n,
    category_acc: mean((t) => (t.grade.category_ok ? 1 : 0)),
    priority_acc: mean((t) => (t.grade.priority_ok ? 1 : 0)),
    both_acc: mean((t) => (t.grade.both_ok ? 1 : 0)),
    tone_mean: judged.length ? judged.reduce((s, t) => s + t.judge.tone, 0) / judged.length : null,
    tone_pass: judged.length ? judged.filter((t) => t.judge.pass).length / judged.length : null,
    judged: judged.length,
    runtime_ms_median: n ? rt[Math.floor((n - 1) / 2)] : null,
    tool_calls_mean: mean((t) => t.tool_calls),
    tool_errors_mean: mean((t) => t.tool_errors),
    tokens_mean: mean((t) => t.input_tokens + t.output_tokens),
    usd: done.reduce((s, t) => s + (t.usd ?? 0), 0),
    excluded: {
      harness_error: list.filter((t) => t.status === 'harness_error').length,
      rate_limited: list.filter((t) => t.status === 'rate_limited').length,
      void: list.filter((t) => t.void).length,
    },
  }
}
// Headline metrics use base trials only, so they match the saved prediction. Top-ups are reported per cell.
const metrics = {}
for (const cfgId of Object.keys(CONFIGS)) metrics[cfgId] = stats(base.filter((t) => t.cfgId === cfgId))
const cellsOut = {}
for (const t of [...base, ...topup]) {
  const c = (cellsOut[t.cell] ??= { base_n: 0, base_pass: 0, topup_n: 0, topup_pass: 0 })
  if (!valid(t)) continue
  if (t.tag === 't') { c.base_n++; if (t.grade.both_ok) c.base_pass++ }
  else { c.topup_n++; if (t.grade.both_ok) c.topup_pass++ }
}
const voided = [...baseScan.voided, ...topScan.voided]

const failing = [...base, ...topup]
  .filter((t) => (valid(t) && (!t.grade.both_ok || (t.judge && !t.judge.pass))) || t.status !== 'completed')
  .slice(0, 80)
  .map((t) => `${t.trialId} status=${t.status} cat_ok=${t.grade?.category_ok} pri_ok=${t.grade?.priority_ok} tone=${t.judge?.tone ?? '-'} file=${RUN_DIR}/${t.trialId}.json${t.error ? ' error=' + t.error : ''}`)
  .join('\n')

const failures = await agent(
  `Do failure analysis for the triage eval, round ${ROUND}. Configs: B is the reference (12-line prompt, 6 tools). C2 is B with tools merged to 3 plus a separate check_status tool.
Failing or excluded trials:
${failing || '(none)'}

Read the runner output files and traces in ${RUN_DIR}, spe/evals/tasks/answers.json, and spe/evals/graders/. Group the failures into types. For each type give name, kind, what, how_to_spot, seen_in (trial IDs), and fix. If a reference label or the grader looks wrong, report it as kind "grader" with the evidence. A harness error or rate limit is kind "harness", not an agent failure. Do not read spe/predictions/ or spe/plans/. Do not edit any file.`,
  { label: 'failure analysis', phase: 'Synthesis', schema: FAILURE_SCHEMA, model: AGENT_MODEL },
)

const critic = await agent(
  `You are the completeness critic for the triage eval, round ${ROUND}. Check this result for gaps. Do not read or edit files.
Expected: ${cells.length} cells, ${TRIALS_PER_CELL} trials each, configs ${Object.keys(CONFIGS).join(', ')}${DRY ? ', dry run' : `, ${EXPECTED_TICKETS} tickets`}.
Metrics per config: ${JSON.stringify(metrics)}
Cells: ${JSON.stringify(cellsOut)}
Voided: ${JSON.stringify(voided)}
Budget: ${JSON.stringify({ cap: budget.cap, spent: budget.spent, skipped: budget.skipped.length })}
Check these points. Every cell has its trials or a logged reason. Every valid base reply was judged. No voided or excluded trial is counted. The cap was not crossed. List any metric where every config is at its maximum as a ceiling metric. List halt reasons: budget skips, voids that point to a leak, grader trouble, or a decision only the user can make.`,
  { label: 'completeness critic', phase: 'Synthesis', schema: CRITIC_SCHEMA, model: AGENT_MODEL },
)

return {
  round: ROUND,
  dry: DRY,
  configs: CONFIGS,
  metrics,
  cells: cellsOut,
  split_cells: split,
  voided,
  budget: { cap: budget.cap, spent: Number(budget.spent.toFixed(2)), skipped: budget.skipped },
  judge_note: 'Opus judge, same family as trials. No other-family judge available.',
  failures: failures.failure_types,
  critic,
  halt: critic.halt_reasons,
}
```
